<title>INDIA: India's G.E. Shipping 96/97 net falls.</title>
<headline>India's G.E. Shipping 96/97 net falls.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-06-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to March 31, 1997.</p>
<p>	     (in million rupees unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit		1,364.2 vs   1,524.0</p>
<p>    Income		    7,812.2 vs   7,252.0</p>
<p>    Other income		872.9 vs     722.1</p>
<p>    Expenditure	     5,250.8 vs   5,187.0</p>
<p>    Operating profit	3,529.9 vs   3,125.4</p>
<p>    Interest		    690.6 vs     453.3</p>
<p>    Gross profit	    2,839.3 vs   2,672.1</p>
<p>    Depreciation	    1,225.1 vs     903.1</p>
<p>    Taxation		    250.0 vs     245.0</p>
<p>Note: The Great Eastern Shipping Co Ltd said its profit from the sale of ships was lower by 242.7 million rupees as the firm sold only one ship in 1996/97 against five in 1995/96. The company said the results were audited.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
